17. My DFS Checklist (Use for Every Graph Problem)

Before coding, ask yourself:

✅ Can I reverse the search?
✅ What are the starting nodes?
✅ What is the DFS condition?
✅ What is my visited structure?
✅ What are the base cases?
✅ When does the function return?
✅ Am I looking for a union or an intersection?

Following this checklist will help you approach not only this problem, but many graph and DFS interview questions systematically.